\p{Let’s see how \sf{Splay} actually works. We find the element #{x} in the tree and then keep moving it up the tree until it reaches the root, according to the following three rules. In general we will use #{p} to denote the parent of #{x} and #{g} to denote its grandparent.  There are three general rules we apply depending on where #{x} is in the tree.}

